import EditorialPage from '../components/EditorialPage.astro';
---
<EditorialPage title="Quality, defined together." eyebrow="Quality assurance" description="A clear specification and an agreed inspection plan provide the basis for evaluating your garments. Discuss measurements, appearance, construction and testing requirements before production.">
<section class="cat-section"><div class="cat-wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Understanding acceptance sampling</p><h2>What AQL actually means.</h2></div></div><div class="option-grid"><article class="option-panel"><h3>The plan comes first</h3><p>Acceptance Quality Limit (AQL) indexes a statistical sampling scheme. The lot size and agreed inspection level determine the sample-size code; the selected plan determines the sample size and acceptance/rejection numbers.</p></article><article class="option-panel"><h3>Classify the defects</h3><p>Critical, major and minor defects need agreed definitions and criteria. The applicable AQL and inspection rules are agreed with the buyer for each class; they are not interchangeable.</p></article><article class="option-panel"><h3>Evaluate the sample</h3><p>The inspector compares the observed count with the plan’s acceptance and rejection numbers. AQL 2.5 does not mean that every inspected sample can contain exactly 2.5% defective garments, nor is it an inspection level or zero-defect guarantee.</p></article></div><p class="mt-6 text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Reference framework: ISO 2859-1 acceptance sampling. The buyer’s agreed plan, including normal/tightened/reduced rules where applicable, governs the inspection.</p></div></section>
<section class="cat-section"><div class="cat-wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Agree the requirements</p><h2>From specification to final review.</h2></div></div><ol class="process-list">{[['01','Reference & measurements','Confirm an approved sample, size specification and construction details.'],['02','Materials & appearance','Define fabric, colour, artwork and trim requirements against the agreed references.'],['03','Production review','Agree the inspection checkpoints and how issues will be recorded and addressed.'],['04','Final inspection','Review finished garments, assortment, labels and packing against the order and buyer’s inspection plan.']].map(([n,title,body])=><li><p class="eyebrow">{n}</p><h3>{title}</h3><p>{body}</p></li>)}</ol></div></section>
<section class="cat-section"><div class="cat-wrap"><h2>Testing should answer a specific question.</h2><div class="option-grid mt-8">{[['Colour & dimensional stability','Specify colourfastness, wash conditions, shrinkage limits and the applicable test methods.'],['Surface & construction','Discuss pilling, strength and seam requirements. Pilling and abrasion are different properties and need the appropriate methods.'],['Safety & documentation','Share chemical, physical and market-specific requirements. Confirm the laboratory, test scope and reports needed for the actual order.']].map(([title,text])=><article class="option-panel"><h3>{title}</h3><p>{text}</p></article>)}</div></div></section>
</EditorialPage>
